  "body": "Given:\r\n\r\n```WebIDL\r\ncallback OnBeforeUnloadEventHandlerNonNull = DOMString? (Event event);\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd relevant spec text:\r\n\r\n> \"If the returnValue attribute of the event object is not the empty string, or if the event was canceled, then the user agent should ask the user to confirm that they wish to unload the document.\"\r\n\r\nIf the event handler returns null, it doesn't currently seem to be used correctly used in the spec text above? Because null \"is not the empty string\". I was expecting:\r\n\r\n> If the returnValue attribute of the event object is **not null** and not the empty string, or if the event was canceled, then the user agent should ask the user to confirm that they wish to unload the document.\r\n\r\nBut maybe I'm missing something? ",
